  <part id="P1">
    <measure number="1" width="150.57">
      <print>
        <system-layout>
          <system-margins>
            <left-margin>205.33</left-margin>
            <right-margin>-0.00</right-margin>
            </system-margins>
          <top-system-distance>70.00</top-system-distance>
          </system-layout>
        </print>
      <attributes>
        <divisions>2</divisions>
        <key>
          <fifths>0</fifths>
          </key>
        <time>
          <beats>4</beats>
          <beat-type>4</beat-type>
          </time>
        <clef>
          <sign>G</sign>
          <line>2</line>
          </clef>
        </attributes>
      <direction placement="above">
        <direction-type>
          <metronome parentheses="no" default-x="-34.80" relative-y="20.00">
            <beat-unit>quarter</beat-unit>
            <per-minute>120</per-minute>
            </metronome>
          </direction-type>
        <sound tempo="120"/>
        </direction>
      <direction placement="below">
        <direction-type>
          <words default-y="-40.00" relative-y="-35.00">Spoken: This is my message to all these Jews out there.
</words>
          <words>If you dont wanna listen, I don't even care.
</words>
          <words>You see, Hanukkah is a time to pray and sing and hang out with families.
</words>
          <words>It's a time to light candles, and forget about your fantasies.
</words>
          <words>While this can be completely strange, so please put on your yarmulke.
</words>
          <words>This is not about Christmas or Kwanzaa or New Years, this is Hanukkah.
</words>
          <words>Some hanukkah traditions are lighting candles and spinning dreidels.
</words>
          <words>So, if you want to do it, go ahead, if you're able.
</words>
          <words>This is not christmas, where we get 1 day of gifts.
</words>
          <words>But for you guys, you each get 8 nights for a lift.
</words>
          <words>But a lot of kids in this town, are not in that religion, you see.
</words>
          <words>They just open presents underneath their Christmas tree.
</words>
          <words>Twas the 25th night of Kislev, and all through the home,
</words>
          <words>People light the candles for the menorah and eat sufganiyot.
</words>
          <words>So, if you guys all want to eat latkes and play dreidel all day..
</words>
          <words>There's only one thing I would say…
</words>
          <words>
</words>
          <words>t</words>
          </direction-type>
        </direction>
      <note>
        <rest measure="yes"/>
        <duration>8</duration>
        <voice>1</voice>
        </note>
      </measure>
